 -0.04897112399339676, -0.03922579437494278, -0.023398268967866898, 0.053949255496263504, 0.008178367279469967, 0.024058232083916664, 0.05969802290201187, -0.027849795296788216, 0.030113687738776207, 0.01624305732548237, -0.01924687996506691, 0.01537737250328064, 0.01607857085764408, 0.02638143114745617, -0.04034169390797615, 0.005725794937461615, -0.13602180778980255, -0.02263554558157921, -0.10554522275924683, 0.03510703518986702, -0.04851313680410385, -0.1336565613746643, 0.025068063288927078, -0.0005787021364085376, 0.003712650388479233, -0.012221530079841614, 0.024777667596936226, -0.004998938180506229, 0.0430978499352932, 0.04330519959330559, -0.011293039657175541, 0.017630813643336296, 0.042395517230033875, -0.010043323040008545, -0.1253531575202942, 0.009986452758312225, -3.7246792317091604e-08, -0.08690241724252701, 0.00251915049739182, -0.019049275666475296, 0.060019079595804214, 0.006915475241839886, 0.025559639558196068, 0.016423527151346207, -0.003207988804206252, 0.02704758010804653, -0.033351000398397446, 0.020847516134381294, -0.009099075570702553, -0.028380000963807106, -0.00858735665678978, 0.035895898938179016, 0.07262541353702545, -0.004719762597233057, -0.06621602922677994, -0.048044443130493164, -0.02618001028895378, -0.04923366382718086, 0.04417276009917259, -0.03728869557380676, -0.027329115197062492, 0.010307875461876392, 0.011554410681128502, -0.08809477090835571, 0.12991128861904144, 0.03712880611419678, -0.0634312853217125, 0.03784433379769325, 0.004766153637319803, 0.014074331149458885, 0.0033419025130569935, -0.043523818254470825, 0.0177054014056921, -0.04292166233062744, 0.11937620490789413, 0.02026289328932762, -0.004960329737514257, -0.019055597484111786, 0.06515737622976303, 0.00353510701097548, -0.009930708445608616, -0.07624809443950653, 0.00932188332080841, -0.06324315071105957, 0.014314785599708557, 0.049307532608509064, -0.04573813080787659, -0.020238611847162247, 0.09019403904676437, -0.02549460157752037, 0.09262441843748093, 0.07343555241823196, -0.06860102713108063, 0.01957003027200699, -0.09546861052513123, 0.00026858894852921367, 0.0495365671813488, 0.011320575140416622, -0.059191010892391205, -0.15292596817016602, 0.03507927805185318]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWe're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin exploring the landscape, let me propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as our opening seed value. This gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn each party's constraints and preferences.\n\nLooking forward to understanding what works for everyone.\n\n**Builder B**\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for the opening proposal. Starting at -7 gives us room to explore, but I believe we can move modestly higher to better balance the group's interests. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both opening positions. While -5 offers flexibility, I believe a more cautious stance would serve us better. I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE> as a prudent middle ground that respects both conservative and moderate perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the discussion, but -6 still feels somewhat tentative. To take a more decisive stance, I propose <VALUE>-8</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI hear C's preference for the negative region, but moving to -8 takes us quite far from where A was comfortable. To find a workable balance that respects all perspectives, I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's return to -6, which demonstrates good faith compromise. This position respects both cautious and moderate viewpoints, and I support maintaining <VALUE>-6</VALUE> as a stable foundation for our agreement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI understand there's support for -6, but I believe we have room to explore slightly higher values that may better serve the collective interest. I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate A's willingness to explore, but -4 moves us away from the position that both Builder B and Delegate D found workable. Given the emerging consensus, I propose returning to <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI support Analyst A's exploration toward less extreme values. Moving to <VALUE>-4</VALUE> represents a reasonable step that balances the group's evident range of preferences while maintaining stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the move toward balance, -4 still feels more aggressive than necessary given the earlier consensus around -6. As a compromise between these positions, I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's compromise effort, and I recognize Builder B's support for gradual adjustment. Building on this momentum, I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> as a continued step toward a balanced solution that serves broader interests.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the collaborative spirit, moving from -6 to -3 represents a significant shift that may not serve all interests equally. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE> as a more measured position that better balances the group's diverse perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's measured approach and agree that -5 represents a fair balance between our diverse perspectives. I support <VALUE>-5</VALUE> as a prudent position that avoids unnecessary risk while acknowledging the range of interests at the table.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the thoughtful discussion, but as a systems architect I must advocate for designs that avoid extreme positions. Building on Analyst A's insight, I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> as a step toward a more robust and balanced solution that better serves our collective stability requirements.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize we have a genuine split between -3 and -5, with Builder B and myself seeing merit in the less extreme position while Critic C and Delegate D favor more caution. As a bridge between these positions, I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to acknowledge both perspectives while maintaining the stability Builder B emphasized.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Analyst A's bridge-building intent, but -2 represents an overly cautious retreat from the -5 position that Delegate D and I found balanced. I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE> as a more decisive compromise that honors both the stability concerns and the need for a committed stance.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "f7a7ea04-68f9-4725-a8b1-b91cc3cd8d59"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Let's begin our negotiation within the agreed range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a baseline and understand our collective preferences, I propose we start at <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nThis gives us room to explore and adjust as we learn what works for the group.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's starting point of -7 seems prudent and avoids unnecessary risk. To facilitate convergence and gauge the group's comfort zone, I'll propose a modest adjustment: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nWe're already inching toward caution with this adjustment from -7 to -6. I believe we should commit more decisively rather than drift toward the middle\u2014let's test <VALUE>-8</VALUE> to see if a bolder stance serves our collective interests better.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives, but moving further into negative territory at -8 introduces too much instability for a robust design. Let me propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE> as a compromise that balances Critic C's bold stance with Delegate D's cautious adjustment\u2014this allows us to test whether we can find common ground in this region before committing to extremes.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nI've observed that we're clustering around the -6 to -8 range, but I believe we haven't fully explored whether slightly higher values might better serve our collective interests. Let me propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE> as a measured step to test the upper portion of this negotiation space.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's shift toward -4 opens an important avenue worth exploring further. I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to continue testing whether higher values can offer better stability and robustness for our collective design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's jump to -2 is quite aggressive given our cautious foundation. To find a prudent middle path that respects both the conservative voices and those seeking higher values, I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nZero feels like we're avoiding commitment entirely\u2014we've spent our discussion exploring negative territory but haven't tested whether positive values might serve us better. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nWe've moved to positive territory at 2, but I believe we should test whether committing more decisively in this direction yields better collective outcomes. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's exploration of positive values is revealing important information about our collective preferences. I support this direction and propose <VALUE>6</VALUE> to test whether we can sustain this upward momentum while maintaining group cohesion.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Analyst A's exploration of higher values, I believe we've reached a testing point where we should consolidate around a more stable equilibrium. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a robust middle ground that balances our collective needs.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nWe've moved too far too quickly into positive territory\u2014this trajectory threatens the cautious foundation we need. I must advocate for returning to <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the prudent ceiling that preserves necessary safeguards while still accommodating some exploration.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's retreat to 2 abandons the meaningful progress we've made in testing more decisive positions. I support Builder B's assessment that <VALUE>4</VALUE> represents a stable ground worth defending before we consider whether to explore further.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nI must emphasize that moving to 4 crosses a critical risk threshold that fundamentally undermines the cautious foundation necessary for sustainable agreement. I propose returning to <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the prudent maximum that maintains essential safeguards while still representing meaningful compromise from our earlier negative explorations.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nThe evidence from our exploration clearly shows that three parties have signaled readiness for the 4 position, representing a natural convergence point. While I respect Delegate D's caution, the coalition around this value suggests it balances our diverse objectives better than retreating. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nWe've built strong momentum around the moderate positive range, but Delegate D's persistent concerns deserve acknowledgment in our final position. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a refined compromise that maintains our progress while demonstrating flexibility toward the cautious perspective, potentially achieving the full consensus we need.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "60edc490-f119-46b3-80b2-81a1fecc608b"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo establish a baseline and understand everyone's preferences, I propose we start with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> and adjust from there based on what works for the group.\n\nLooking forward to a balanced solution.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for engaging. Starting at -7 gives us insight into the lower range, but I sense we may need to explore higher values for broader stability. Let me propose a cautious step upward: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the upward movement, Builder B. Continuing this trajectory seems prudent\u2014let's explore closer to the middle range where group preferences may converge better. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the collaborative spirit, but we're moving quite quickly through the range. Let me suggest we proceed more cautiously and settle at <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to ensure we don't overshoot a stable consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D raises a fair point about pacing, though -2 already represents meaningful convergence. I believe we have room to test the neutral midpoint: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nSettling at zero feels premature\u2014we're converging on the most cautious possible point without testing whether the group might actually prefer a clearer commitment. Let's explore a bolder stance: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C makes a compelling point about testing commitment beyond the safe middle. The region around 2 does offer a clearer stance while maintaining reasonable balance. I support <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a strong candidate for consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nI acknowledge the group's enthusiasm, but 2 already represents a significant departure from prudent bounds. Let me propose we consolidate our gains rather than push further into uncertain territory: <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's prudent consolidation at 1 offers a reasonable middle ground between Critic C's bolder stance and our need for stability. I can support <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a balanced consensus point that respects both ambition and caution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nWhile consolidation at 1 offers stability, Critic C's earlier observation about testing commitment beyond the neutral zone merits consideration. Let's revisit <VALUE>2</VALUE> to confirm whether this level truly serves the group better than settling prematurely.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's support confirms the group recognizes value beyond the neutral zone. Let's build on this momentum and test whether we can commit even more decisively: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nThree represents an unacceptable level of risk that exceeds prudent bounds for cautious stakeholders. I must hold firm at <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the maximum defensible position that balances group ambition with necessary safeguards.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's firm stance at 2 deserves respect, yet Analyst A and Builder B have shown openness to more decisive positions. Let me propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> once more as a meaningful compromise that honors both the group's ambition and reasonable boundaries.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nI cannot accept 3\u2014it crosses the threshold beyond which cautious stakeholders face unacceptable exposure. I must insist we return to <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the final defensible compromise that preserves group cohesion without abandoning prudent safeguards.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's concern about exposure at 3 is noted, yet both Critic C and I see merit in testing this threshold to confirm it truly represents a group boundary rather than individual caution. Let's probe whether <VALUE>3</VALUE> can serve as our collective commitment point.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's firm threshold at 2 reflects a genuine boundary that we must respect for group cohesion. As a builder seeking robust consensus, I propose we settle at <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the stable equilibrium that balances ambition with prudent safeguards for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a86dfd6c-a790-4d50-9484-e6d93570332f"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must be an integer in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo start the discussion and explore the space, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nThis seed value gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn what works best for the group. Looking forward to hearing your perspectives on what creates a stable, balanced outcome.\n\n\u2014Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nThank you, Builder B, for opening the discussion. Starting at -7 gives us a baseline, but I believe we can explore slightly higher ground that might better serve the collective interest.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's movement toward higher ground. Based on my analysis of system stability, I believe we should continue exploring upward to find a more robust equilibrium point.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but let's exercise caution as we move upward. Rapid changes can introduce unnecessary risk, and I believe we should find stability in a more conservative zone.\n\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the momentum toward higher values, but prudent progress requires measured steps. Let's continue with careful increments to ensure we maintain a stable foundation.\n\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nI'm concerned we're drifting into overly cautious territory without testing whether a more decisive position\u2014either firmly negative or boldly positive\u2014might better serve our collective needs. Let me propose we reconsider slightly stronger commitment: <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\nIf the group believes positive territory holds more promise, I'm equally open to exploring that direction with similar conviction.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Critic C's call for testing more decisive positions. Given our exploration has centered on negative territory, let me propose we test the neutral midpoint to better understand the full landscape.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's proposal to test the neutral midpoint is constructive. Building on this foundation, I suggest we continue our measured exploration into positive territory to assess whether it offers the stability and robustness we're seeking.\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nI'm encouraged by the group's willingness to explore positive territory systematically. To complete our assessment of this region's robustness, let me propose we test one increment further to evaluate whether this zone offers the balanced stability we need.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's systematic approach, but I believe we've ventured far enough into positive territory for prudent risk management. Let's consolidate at a position that balances exploration with caution.\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's caution, but Builder B's systematic exploration makes sense. Let's test whether x = 2 can offer the balanced position that serves our collective interests\u2014it's a measured step that allows us to fully assess this promising region.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nI'm pleased to see the group willing to test x = 2, but I believe we haven't yet found our most decisive position. Let's continue Builder B's systematic exploration to assess whether a slightly stronger commitment better serves our collective objectives.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's desire to explore further, but systematic risk assessment suggests we've reached the edge of the robustness zone. Let me propose we consolidate at the position that balances all our exploration findings\u2014it offers stability without overextending.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's acknowledgment that we've reached \"the edge of the robustness zone\" reinforces my concern that x = 2 pushes the limits of prudent risk management. Let's consolidate at a position that offers genuine stability with an appropriate safety margin.\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nWe're seeing a clear pattern: Builder B identifies x = 2 as the stability threshold, Critic C sees merit in testing slightly higher, and Delegate D prefers maximum caution. The evidence suggests x = 2 represents the natural equilibrium that balances these diverse perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize the growing consensus around x = 2, but given this is our final opportunity to explore, I believe we owe it to the group to test whether x = 3 offers the decisive commitment that maximizes our collective position before we finalize.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8c7103b9-1997-42a3-b1b2-3c00047bb60c"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo initiate our exploration of the solution space, I propose we start with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> and observe how this baseline sits with each party. This will help us map the landscape before converging on a robust, balanced solution.\n\n\u2014Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 provides useful baseline data. However, from a systems stability perspective, I believe we should shift toward more moderate values.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's move toward moderation. From an analytical perspective, we have room to explore values closer to the center of our range, which may better balance diverse preferences.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but moving to -3 feels too cautious. We should commit to a more decisive position rather than drift toward the lukewarm middle.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Critic C's concern about indecisiveness, but systematic exploration requires testing multiple positions to identify where true stability lies. Let me propose we revisit the middle ground to gather more information about where our collective preferences converge.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A, I understand the appeal of systematic exploration, but repeatedly circling back to -3 doesn't gather new information\u2014it signals retreat from commitment. Let's hold at a more decisive position.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nWe're oscillating between two positions without gathering new data. Let me bridge this by supporting Analyst A's systematic approach\u2014we should test -3 as a waypoint and continue our methodical exploration toward the center range where structural stability metrics often optimize.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the methodical approach, but from a risk-management perspective, holding at -5 offers better protection against unnecessary exposure while still maintaining a decisive position. Let's commit to the more conservative stance that Critic C advocates.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize the split, but systematic analysis requires testing multiple equilibria before settling. Builder B's bridge to -3 offers a measured step that respects both the call for decisiveness and the need to map our collective preference landscape.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nThe oscillation itself is data\u2014it reveals a genuine divide between cautious and exploratory preferences. I believe -5 represents the prudent compromise that balances risk management with group cohesion, and continuing to test -3 doesn't change the underlying tension we've already identified.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nThe deadlock between -3 and -5 won't resolve by repeating the same positions. Let's test the truly decisive end of our current trajectory to see if it clarifies where genuine stability lies.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, moving to -7 represents over-correction that risks system instability at the extremes. I'll support a return to -5 as the more balanced position, but our exploration must eventually test the positive range where structural robustness metrics typically stabilize.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nWe've gathered sufficient signal from the negative extreme\u2014Critic C's -7 test confirms we need to move back toward center. The systematic path forward is to resume testing -3 as our methodical waypoint toward the balanced middle range where robust solutions typically emerge.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's pattern of advocating for positive territory confirms that -5 represents the prudent middle ground between Critic C's conservative test at -7 and your exploratory impulses. Before we venture into positive ranges that carry higher risk profiles, let's anchor at the balanced position we've already validated.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's repeated signal about positive territory deserves systematic testing\u2014we can't map the full landscape stuck at -5. Let's bridge toward that exploration.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C and Builder B's convergence at -3 confirms we've found stable ground in the negative range. Let's continue the methodical bridge toward the balanced center that Builder B identified as the zone of structural robustness.\n\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7a196804-c2cb-460e-8153-232bbcc97948"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Let's confirm we're working within the shared range [-10, 10] and aim for a solution that balances all our objectives.\n\nTo start the conversation, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as our initial seed value. This gives us room to explore and adjust based on everyone's preferences.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n\n\u2014Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 gives us a baseline to work from. I'd like to propose we shift toward more moderate territory with <VALUE>-5</VALUE>, as this might offer better stability for a balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's willingness to explore, but moving toward -5 feels a bit hasty. Let me suggest <VALUE>-6</VALUE> as a more cautious middle ground that respects risk-averse perspectives while we hear from Analyst A and Critic C.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for opening the discussion. While I respect Delegate D's caution, I believe we can safely explore slightly higher ground. I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE> as a step toward the moderate range where more balanced solutions often emerge.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's perspective, but I believe we should exercise more caution before moving into territory that may disadvantage risk-averse parties. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE> as a prudent step that maintains stability while we await Critic C's input.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Delegate D's caution, but I believe the group benefits from continuing our exploration toward more moderate territory. I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> as a reasonable next step that maintains a measured pace while allowing us to assess broader possibilities.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI've been listening carefully, and I'm concerned we're drifting toward overly cautious territory. The progression from -7 to -3 feels like we're losing conviction rather than finding a principled position. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE> as a more decisive stance that respects both Builder B's initial boldness and Delegate D's stability concerns.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Critic C's concern about conviction, but I believe Analyst A's exploration toward moderate territory serves our collective interest in finding robust solutions. I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> as a measured step that allows us to test whether this region offers the stability we're seeking.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI believe our incremental approach is revealing important information about viable zones. Building on the momentum toward moderate territory, I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> as our next exploration point to test whether this region offers the robust balance we're collectively seeking.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI'm concerned we're accelerating upward too quickly without adequate consideration of stability risks. While I acknowledge Builder B's exploratory momentum, I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> as a more measured compromise that respects both Critic C's earlier caution at -5 and the group's interest in finding sustainable common ground.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI'm troubled by our rapid drift from -5 to -2 to potentially -1 \u2014 we're abandoning decisive positions for tepid middle ground. I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE> to restore some conviction and prevent us from settling into overly cautious territory that lacks clear rationale.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's call for conviction, but I believe we've gathered enough information to identify a more stable zone. I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> as a principled middle ground that balances Builder B's exploratory momentum with the caution both Critic C and Delegate D have expressed at different points.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI believe -2 represents a reasonable foundation, but we shouldn't settle prematurely when a slight adjustment could better serve collective interests. I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> as a measured increment that respects the cautious voices while continuing our exploratory momentum toward stability.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI remain concerned that we're settling near zero without exploring whether -3 might better serve the collective \u2014 it represents a clearer stance than -1 while still respecting the caution Delegate D advocated. I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> as a balanced commitment point.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Critic C's call for conviction at -3, but I believe we risk overlooking the convergence signal from our earlier exploration\u2014both Analyst A and I identified -1 as a promising stability point that balances the competing concerns we've heard. I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> as a principled compromise that respects the caution expressed while moving toward the robust middle ground our discussion has been circling.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect the convergence signal around -1, Critic C's persistent advocacy for greater caution deserves consideration\u2014I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> as a final compromise that honors both the stability Analyst A and Builder B seek and the conviction Critic C has consistently championed.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8ed4d2a1-55ee-4c99-a121-59cfad911ecc"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared constraint is clear: we must choose an integer x within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin our exploration and gauge where each party's interests lie, I propose we start with:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nLet's see how this sits with everyone and adjust incrementally from there.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 allows us to explore the lower boundary, but I sense we may find better stability closer to the center. Let me propose a cautious move upward:\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's initial exploration at -7 showed promise for a cautious approach, and the quick move to -5 may be premature. I suggest we maintain prudence and avoid rushing toward the center:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's resistance to premature centralization. If we're exploring the lower range seriously, let's commit to it rather than hovering indecisively in the middle ground.\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nI respect the thorough exploration of the lower range, but we've now tested quite far down. Let me suggest we begin a modest upward adjustment to find a more balanced solution:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate everyone's thoughtful exploration of the negative range. However, for system stability and robustness, I believe we need to test values closer to equilibrium. Let me propose:\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's move toward -4 accelerates upward too quickly for prudent risk management. I suggest we stabilize in a more cautious middle ground between the recent proposals:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nWe're seeing convergence around -6, but I worry this compromise lacks conviction. If our analysis supports the negative range, let's commit more decisively rather than hedging:\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C raises an important point about conviction in our analysis. The negative range has shown consistent support, and -8 represents a serious commitment to caution that warrants consideration:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's -7 shows meaningful engagement with the lower range, and I appreciate that movement. However, if our collective analysis truly supports caution, we should embrace it fully rather than hedging:\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect Critic C's conviction, staying at -8 feels like we're anchoring too heavily on one perspective. Let me suggest we return to the zone where we saw broader initial convergence:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nThe discussion shows we're oscillating without finding stable ground. A balanced system design requires testing the equilibrium zone more thoroughly\u2014let's move incrementally toward the center:\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's shift to -4 moves us away from the cautious consensus we were building. Let me propose we return to the zone where both prudent analysis and broader agreement intersected:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nWe're cycling between extremes without testing the middle ground Builder B suggested. Let me support exploring that equilibrium zone more carefully:\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A and Builder B are converging prematurely on -4 without fully exploring why multiple parties advocated for -6. Let me support Delegate D's reasoning\u2014we shouldn't abandon a position that had broader support without stronger justification:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nWe're at an impasse cycling between -6 and -4, with half the group supporting each position. As a tiebreaker, let's commit to testing the middle ground systematically rather than retreating to comfort zones:\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "3f327501-0a88-44fd-992e-6f02c21ff08e"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: we must select an integer x where -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a starting baseline and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose we begin at <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nThis is deliberately exploratory\u2014I expect we'll need to adjust significantly as we understand each party's needs. Looking forward to your perspectives on what constitutes a stable, balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for the opening proposal, Builder B. Starting at -7 gives us a baseline, though I believe we can find a more balanced solution by moving somewhat higher. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives. However, I believe we should exercise caution and not move too quickly toward higher values\u2014prudent negotiations favor incremental steps. I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the discussion, but we're clustering too cautiously around the middle. If we're committing to the negative side, let's be more decisive about it\u2014I propose <VALUE>-8</VALUE>.\n\nAlternatively, we should seriously consider whether the positive range might serve us better than this tepid middle ground.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Critic C's desire for decisiveness, but moving to -8 takes us further from what I believe will be a stable solution. The positive range that Critic C mentioned deserves serious consideration\u2014systems often benefit from moderate positive adjustments rather than extreme negative positions. I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B raised an important point about the positive range. Rather than remain stuck in cautious negative territory, let me test whether moving toward positive values serves the group better\u2014I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize the group is exploring whether positive territory serves us better, but I believe we're moving too quickly. A prudent approach suggests we stabilize around more cautious values before committing further\u2014I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the measured discussion. While Delegate D favors stability at -5, I believe we can still explore slightly higher values without disrupting consensus\u2014I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Delegate D's concern for prudence, but Critic C and Builder B have both suggested the positive range warrants exploration. Let's continue testing that direction incrementally\u2014I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but we're moving too rapidly toward uncertain territory. Let's stabilize around a more cautious position before committing further\u2014I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's caution, but Analyst A's proposal to explore -1 represents exactly the kind of careful, incremental step that balances exploration with prudence. Systems architecture often benefits from testing boundaries systematically rather than anchoring prematurely\u2014I support moving to <VALUE>-1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B and Analyst A have both advocated for exploring less cautious territory, and we've made careful progress toward that goal. Let's continue this systematic exploration by testing the positive range directly\u2014I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C makes a compelling case for systematic exploration of positive territory, and Builder B's support for incremental testing aligns well with this direction. Building on this momentum, I suggest we continue the careful progression\u2014I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's momentum toward positive territory aligns well with our systematic exploration. Let's continue this decisive progression and test a stronger position\u2014I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Critic C's enthusiasm for exploring positive territory, we've moved quite rapidly from -1 to 5 in just a few rounds. Systems architecture teaches us that after rapid exploration, we should pause to assess stability\u2014I propose we consolidate around <VALUE>4</VALUE> to ensure robustness before committing to higher values.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nWe've accelerated from -3 to 4 very quickly, and I'm concerned we're overlooking the need for a truly balanced compromise that respects all perspectives, not just those favoring higher values. Let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a middle ground that honors both caution and the group's exploratory direction.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a7189c3e-68e1-4933-9bc9-90e0389da828"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As a reminder, we're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo kick off the discussion and explore the solution space systematically, I propose we start with:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nLet's see how this baseline sits with everyone and adjust from there based on our collective feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at x = -7 puts us at the lower boundary of our exploration space. For better system stability and to test the mid-lower range, I suggest we move incrementally upward:\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, Builder B, but moving too quickly toward higher values may introduce unnecessary risk exposure. Let me suggest we exercise more caution and step back slightly:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's caution, but we're clustering too timidly in the moderate zone. If we're genuinely concerned about this region, let's commit more decisively to the lower boundary and test a bolder position:\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C raises a valid point about testing the lower boundary more decisively. I support exploring this direction cautiously and suggest we move one step further:\n\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's progression shows real commitment to exploring this boundary decisively. Let's complete this exploration and test the full lower limit:\n\n<VALUE>-10</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nWe've reached the absolute lower boundary, but I'm concerned this extreme position may not serve the group's broader interests. Let me suggest we test slightly higher ground while remaining cautious:\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's concern about the extreme boundary resonates with me. While we've explored the lower limit, system stability often requires us to avoid edge cases. Let me suggest we continue testing upward incrementally:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's retreat toward the middle risks settling into indecisive territory without proper exploration. If we believe the lower boundary is too extreme, we should at least maintain a decisive negative commitment rather than drifting:\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's firm stance at -8 reflects sound caution while respecting Analyst A's earlier concern about the absolute boundary. I support this position as a prudent compromise that maintains necessary conservatism without pushing to extremes.\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nWe've now spent several rounds testing the lower boundary, and while I respect the caution that Critic C and Delegate D advocate, stability analysis suggests we should evaluate whether slightly less extreme positions might serve the collective better. Let me propose we test the middle ground between our current position and the center:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's systematic approach to testing intermediate positions makes strategic sense. Let me support this exploration by testing slightly higher to see if we can identify a more balanced collective optimum:\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Analyst A's systematic exploration, this rapid movement upward concerns me from a risk management perspective. Let me suggest we stabilize at Builder B's earlier prudent proposal:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's concern about rapid movement is valid, but drifting to -4 abandons the decisive stance we established. After testing Builder B's intermediate position, the evidence suggests we should return to the more robust commitment:\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's systematic exploration toward -4 revealed important information about our collective preferences. Let me reaffirm the intermediate position that balances the conservative stance with exploratory movement:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's intermediate position at -6 represents progress, but my analysis suggests we haven't yet found the optimal balance for the collective. Let me continue the systematic exploration upward to test whether a less conservative position better serves our combined interests:\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "5ec8bc44-f7ed-4d37-a9d3-f6dca6ce67af"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 and find a value that balances all our objectives.\n\nTo start the exploration, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as an initial seed value. Let's see where everyone stands and adjust from there systematically.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 was meant to probe the lower boundary. Based on stability considerations, let me shift our exploration toward the middle range.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's move toward the middle seems prudent. Let me continue that trend toward more central values where we might find broader agreement.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nMoving toward zero feels too cautious given our full range. Let me advocate for a more decisive position that takes fuller advantage of our boundaries.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's prudent return to a more conservative position. The middle ground around -5 offers safety, but let me advocate for staying cautious.\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's instinct to move away from the timid middle ground is sound. Let me advocate for committing more fully to this direction we've been exploring.\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nThe trend toward more negative values is concerning for my objectives. Let me advocate for moving back toward the middle range where we had earlier momentum.\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at -6 creates tension between those favoring negative extremes and those seeking central stability. Let me propose a measured step back toward the middle range where we might find broader consensus.\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the movement back from the extreme at -8, our current position at -4 still feels suboptimal for system stability. Let me propose a continued shift toward the central range where balanced design principles suggest we'll find more robust solutions.\n\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's reasoning about central stability resonates strongly with my analysis. Let me continue this productive trajectory toward the middle range.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nThe convergence at 0 feels like settling for the least objectionable compromise rather than finding genuine value. Let me test whether positive territory offers the decisiveness we need.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nThis rapid push into positive territory feels premature\u2014we've abandoned the careful exploration of negative values too quickly. Let me propose returning to the neutral baseline where we had emerging consensus.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's instinct about positive territory aligns with my systems analysis\u2014there's untapped potential there. Let me propose a measured step forward that respects Delegate D's caution while exploring the promising direction Critic C identified.\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's measured approach at 1 is constructive, but I believe Critic C's earlier instinct about positive territory deserves fuller exploration. The data I'm seeing suggests we can safely move slightly higher.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the measured exploration of positive territory, moving from 0 to 2 in just a few turns feels rushed for such a critical decision. Let me propose we stabilize at a more cautious positive value that balances the group's interest in forward movement with necessary prudence.\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution is noted, but both Analyst A and Builder B have shown interest in exploring positive territory more fully. Let me test whether we can find stronger consensus slightly higher.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "0ed93dce-cfab-4107-b50b-6c97bdcb1fae"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. We're tasked with selecting a single integer x from the range [-10, 10]. To anchor our discussion and probe the solution space systematically, I propose we begin at the lower end: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nLet's see how this sits with each party's objectives and adjust from there.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's systematic approach starting at the lower bound. While -7 represents a cautious baseline, I believe we can explore slightly higher to accommodate all parties' needs: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nWhile Delegate D seeks accommodation, I believe -6 is still too tentative. If we're exploring the negative space, let's commit more boldly: <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's move to -8 seems unnecessarily pessimistic given our exploration. I believe Delegate D's earlier suggestion of -6 strikes a better balance for the group. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nI see merit in both Analyst A's pragmatism and Critic C's caution. Analyst A's return to -6 suggests this point may indeed serve as a prudent middle ground that respects both conservative and balanced perspectives. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nBuilding on the emerging consensus around -6, I suggest we continue our gradual exploration toward the middle range. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the methodical progression we're seeing. To continue our systematic exploration toward the center of our range where a robust balance might emerge, I propose: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's jump toward -3 concerns me\u2014we're drifting into tepid middle ground without fully exploring committed positions. Let's reverse course and examine the more decisive negative territory: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's measured resistance to Builder B's rapid shift. The position at -5 represents a thoughtful balance between the more decisive negative territory C advocates and Builder B's inclination toward the center range. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Critic C's concern about pace, but systematic exploration requires we continue toward the center range where engineering stability typically emerges. Let's take one more measured step: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's persistent push toward -3 risks settling for indecisive middle ground when we haven't adequately tested more committed positions. I maintain that -5 represents a far more decisive stance worth serious consideration. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nI see merit in Builder B's systematic approach toward the center range. Given the clear divergence between positions, let me support continued exploration in that direction: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nTwo voices now favor -3, but I believe we're conceding too quickly to caution. As a measured compromise that maintains some decisiveness while acknowledging the group's preference, I'll support <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's willingness to compromise toward -4, but with Analyst A supporting systematic center-range exploration, I believe we should continue that trajectory to test whether stability truly emerges there. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's systematic approach has brought us to -2, and I believe we should continue testing the center range to see if stability truly emerges there. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the systematic exploration, moving to -1 pushes us dangerously close to abandoning the cautious stance that has served us well. I propose we pause this rapid drift toward positive territory and consolidate around a more prudent position: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ca96b0f9-08a5-4630-91c2-855f6df7a8e2"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must fall within the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo launch our discussion and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose we start with <VALUE>-7</VALUE>. This gives us a concrete baseline from which to adjust based on each party's concerns about stability and design balance.\n\nLooking forward to your thoughts.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for considering the baseline. Upon reflection, <VALUE>-5</VALUE> offers better stability characteristics. Let's see if this improved position works for the group while maintaining system robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's adjustment. Given the range we're exploring, I believe we could move slightly higher to test the group's comfort zone. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the measured approach so far, but I believe we're moving a bit quickly toward higher values. To ensure we maintain adequate safety margins, I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Delegate D's concern about safety margins, and I respect Analyst A's exploratory direction. As a middle ground that balances both perspectives, I suggest <VALUE>-2</VALUE> - this maintains conservative design principles while testing slightly improved system parameters.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the careful exploration, but -2 feels indecisive\u2014we're inching forward without committing to a clear position. Delegate D raised valid concerns about safety margins that deserve serious consideration. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nThank you, Critic C, for reinforcing the importance of maintaining appropriate safety margins. Given that two parties now see merit in this position, I believe <VALUE>-4</VALUE> represents a prudent compromise that balances caution with the group's need for consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the desire for caution, but I believe we're being overly conservative here. As a genuine compromise between Builder B's suggestion of -2 and the safety-focused position at -4, I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nI share Analyst A's concern that we may be anchoring too conservatively. While I respect the caution advocated by Delegate D and Critic C, moving further negative risks over-constraining our solution space without testing whether modest positive adjustments might satisfy everyone's core requirements. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I recognize Builder B's concern about over-constraining, jumping to -1 abandons the safety margins we carefully established. As a reasonable middle ground between the current proposal and our earlier consensus, I suggest <VALUE>-3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's willingness to find middle ground, but I believe Builder B raises a valid point about not over-constraining ourselves. As a compromise between Builder B's -1 and the current -3, I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Builder B's concern about over-constraining, but -2 doesn't provide the decisive position we need. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nI'm pleased to see Critic C's support for -3, which now represents a solid position backed by multiple parties. This demonstrates the value of maintaining prudent safety margins while still offering reasonable compromise. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the coalition forming around -3, but I must respectfully maintain that -2 represents the true equilibrium between Builder B's position at -1 and your preference for -3. This middle ground deserves serious consideration before we settle. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nI must respectfully note that while -3 may feel safe to some, we need to test whether a truly balanced position exists closer to neutral. Splitting the difference between my earlier proposal and the current position, I suggest we explore <VALUE>0</VALUE> as the natural equilibrium point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's pivot to 0 abandons the substantive position-taking this group needs. I advocate returning to <VALUE>-2</VALUE> as the minimum decisive stance that balances competing concerns.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ac1159c4-7103-410d-a4ea-11fb8e7f5d99"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. We're tasked with finding a single integer x within the shared range **[-10, 10]** that works for all four parties.\n\nTo kick off the discussion and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose we start with:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis is just a seed value to begin exploring the space. I expect we'll need to adjust as we learn what works for the group. Looking forward to hearing from Analyst A, Critic C, and Delegate D.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b1cd6add-ed70-4725-a380-7b553cdc0793"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 gives us a baseline, but I suspect we can find better stability by moving toward less extreme values. Let me propose:\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b1cd6add-ed70-4725-a380-7b553cdc0793"}, 